From: Bryan B <bbigari@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 01:52:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Expose GSC regex filter operators in search performance

Google's Search Analytics API supports includingRegex and excludingRegex
(RE2), but the app only surfaced equals/notEquals/contains/notContains.
Regex is the only way to isolate machine-issued queries, whose text carries
syntax humans rarely type: exact-match quotes, markdown, search operators.

Widen the operator list, the filter and search-param schemas, and the match
dropdown. The MCP tool picks this up for free because its Zod schema derives
from GSC_FILTER_OPERATORS.

The added test asserts a regex expression reaches the request byte-for-byte;
escaping or rewriting it would silently change what matches.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JTBKYzux1gqV8tvd3Q9XBN
